<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anand Rao Puar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1749">1749</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Anand Rao Pawar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anand Rao Puar was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> commander who took part in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> in the 1720s and 1730s. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baji-rao-i">Baji Rao I</a> confirmed him in possession of Dhar, the old Paramara capital, making him the founder of the Puar princely house of Dhar. His descendants ruled the state until it joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948.</p></div>
